/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  DRYER -- twin-bed 4A molecular sieve (one bed adsorbs while the other
  regenerates).  Takes the ~315 ppm the knock-out drum leaves down below 1 ppm.

  Why that deep?  Because the iron catalyst in the converter tolerates less
  than ~5 ppm of oxygen compounds -- and the simulator does NOT see poisoning:
  delete this block and the case still runs, with the water travelling through
  the loop and into the product.  The dryer is here because the catalyst data
  sheet says so; the case shows you HOW MUCH water it removes.

  `mAdsPerColumn` is a SIZING decision, not a datum: the model refuses the
  feed if the cycle's working capacity is not enough.  Read
  `capacity_utilisation_water` in the report.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
type      tsaTwinBed;
operation
{
    adsorbent      molSieve4A;           // constant/adsorbents/
    mAdsPerColumn  1500 kg;
    tCycle         43200 s;              // 12 h of adsorption per bed
    T_ads          279 K;
    T_regen        553 K;                // 280 C
    lightKey       H2;
    purgeRatio     0.005;
}
boundary  { inlets ( Feed );  outlets ( Dry  Regen ); }
